cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Duetsheet, please cite it as below."
title: "Duetsheet: an interactive report that humans and AI agents review and revise together"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Shu Chi
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ashur5457/duetsheet"
url: "https://github.com/Ashur5457/duetsheet"
abstract: >-
  Duetsheet is an open-source, single-file interactive HTML report for
  human-in-the-loop review of AI-generated, data-heavy reports. People edit
  text and charts in place and annotate figures with boxes, lassos and data
  points stored in data coordinates; every change is recorded with its author
  and grouped into review rounds. The report is plain JSON with a published
  JSON Schema, so any LLM agent can read the feedback and revise the report.
  Raw data keeps its provenance (path and SHA-256), and the figure style can
  be learned from the user's own figures.
keywords:
  - human-in-the-loop
  - AI agents
  - LLM
  - interactive report
  - annotation
  - change tracking
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - scientific workflow
  - data visualization
